  "Question": "An unfair coin has probability \\(p\\) of coming up heads on a single toss. Let \\(w\\) be the probability that, in \\(5\\) independent tosses of this coin, heads come up exactly \\(3\\) times. If \\(w=\\frac{144}{625},\\) then",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(p\\) must be \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)",
    "B": "\\(p\\) must be \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)",
    "C": "\\(p\\) must be greater than \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)",
    "D": "\\(p\\) is not uniquely determined",
    "E": "there is no value of \\(p\\) for which \\(w=\\frac{144}{625}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
